method.description:
The controlling peer owns the value and only the server sees it. Use it for player input.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_property(self, &"move_dir").input()

func _physics_process(dt: float) -> void:
    if entity.is_controlled_locally:
        move_dir = Input.get_vector("left", "right", "up", "down")
    velocity = move_dir * SPEED
[/codeblock]
Each send also includes the last two ticks of input, so the next packet makes up for a lost one. [method windowed] changes how many. Correction settings such as [method extrapolate] are ignored on an input.
